From d4921026ecdb808ee9bb20d5b10bd4eac8c2fc87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:44:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Play the meteor storm's eighth meteor wave at frame 180, as
 the original

rag_meteor_storm_waves (RagEffect 90) played wizard_meteo.wav at frame
170; the original plays it at 180. The original's RagEffect process
switch (0x6f874d) jumps on the effect ID through the table at 0x6ffd94,
whose entry 90 is 0x6fe37d. That case switches on the frame through
0x700540/0x700550: frame 0 plays wizard_meteo and runs on into frame
10's hunter_blastmine, and frames 20, 50, 80, 100, 130, 140, 180 and
200 play wizard_meteo. The unreferenced copy at 0x6eb310 has the same
cases, and so does the cue list of effect 0x48a (0x996ad5), which the
port already has with 180 (ez2str_effect.c).

The fall-through from frame 0 into frame 10, which plays two waves at
frame 0, is the original's and is kept; it now says so.

The new test_meteor_storm_waves runs the extracted function for frames
0-300 with the waves and quake messages recorded and compares them with
the original's schedule: both waves at 0, blast mine at 10, meteo at
20-200 including 180, and a quake every 50 frames from 50 to 250. It
fails on the previous code (170 instead of 180).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
